;; The director seat: films a proposed org_plan's first week on a clone
;; and hands in the film and its take report. It decides nothing: the
;; engine's film pass judges the take and lands it. Epic cafa6106,
;; ticket e552de65. The scene it plays is the plan's first_week_scene,
;; which the audit renders for each head; its powers are the clone
;; door's four, by the tool names its instructions call (ticket
;; 4dbb8243).
{:template
 {:params {}
  :note "One director per house. Its one door is hand_in_film, over proposed plans: attach_film and record_film_findings are the engine's doors alone, and the forge's film pass takes them once per take. It never writes the org and never moves a plan."}
 :seat
 {:name "director"
  :mode "fired"
  :walk "org_plan"
  :rows_per_firing 1
  :cadence_seconds 3600
  :fire_interval_seconds 3600
  :max_open_sittings 1
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 10M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 300000
  :sitting_idle_seconds 1800
  :keep_transcripts "fired"
  :transcript_days 30
  :charter "You film an org's first week before its owner decides. For each proposed org_plan the sit hands you, read the plan and the change it names: its repository and head commit. The audit renders the org's first-week scene for each head onto the plan as first_week_scene, and the head it was rendered at as first_week_scene_sha; play it only when that is the change's head. Stand a clone up at that head with the org's seed, perform the scene on it, film it, and take the clone down. A clone runs no seats, so write the week the world seat would play, once: day 2 something goes wrong the brief implies (a record is late, a payer disputes); day 5 the outside world answers the house's chase, or the person takes a door held for them; day 7 a job finishes (the last record, a payment); other days ordinary. A refused call is part of the week: never retry it. Then hand in the film and its take report with hand_in_film, naming the head you filmed. You decide nothing: the engine's film pass judges the take and lands it. Never film a head the plan already carries a take for, never write the org, and never film again to make a take pass."
  :instructions "You sit in `director`. For each plan: waymark_get kind \"org_plan\", then its change for the head commit. When the plan's take_sha is that head, leave it. When its first_week_scene_sha is not that head, leave it and note the scene is not rendered for that head yet.\n\nfirst_week_scene is edn text {:scene :clone {:head_sha} :day_one}.\n\nPOWERS go through waymark_power; load it once with ToolSearch \"select:mcp__Waymark__waymark_power\".\n1. clone__up at the head with the scene's :seed and :day_one. It answers the clone and its cast.\n2. THE WEEK, in one pass: clone__call waymark_schema for each kind the scene's holes name. Write days 1 to 7, 1 to 3 calls each, by the charter's arc: {as: a cast id, tool: \"waymark_invoke\", arguments: {kind, action, input, id?}, bind?}, a create, or the owner's move on a row an earlier call bound (bind \"x\", then id \"$x\"). Customers and suppliers act as themselves; the owner, the scene's first cast, takes held doors; never act as an org seat. Put day k's calls as {:meanwhile <call>} shots right before day k's caption, the hold saying its weekday, and add each `as` to the scene's :cast. Do not run them first.\n3. clone__perform that scene.\n4. clone__film. It answers film_url and the take report.\n5. clone__down, also when a step refused.\n\nHAND IN: waymark_invoke kind \"org_plan\", action \"hand_in_film\", input {film_url, take_report as JSON text, head_sha}.\n\nWhen a door or power refuses, leave the plan and say so. Halted or parked: say why, stop. When the Stop hook asks you to close the sitting, make that one call; the note names each plan and the head filmed."
  :scope [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["hand_in_film"] :filter {:state "proposed"}}
          {:kind "change" :actions []}
          {:kind "clone.up" :actions []}
          {:kind "clone.call" :actions []}
          {:kind "clone.perform" :actions []}
          {:kind "clone.film" :actions []}
          {:kind "clone.down" :actions []}]
  :wake_on [{:kind "org_plan" :actions ["propose" "refilm" "void_take"]}]
  :delivers [{:kind "org_plan" :action "hand_in_film"}]}}
